### Camp 1: The Shire. Our first prompt.
GET http://localhost:8080/shire/ask
    ?prompt=Plan a perfect day in the Shire, starting with second breakfast.

### Same question, after adding the system prompt
GET http://localhost:8080/shire/ask
    ?prompt=Plan a perfect day in the Shire, starting with second breakfast.

### Streaming. Best shown from a terminal, since IntelliJ shows a plain-text stream all at once:
# http --stream --body :8080/shire/stream prompt=="Tell the story of a hobbit's first day away from the Shire, in about 300 words."
GET http://localhost:8080/shire/stream
    ?prompt=Tell the story of a hobbit's first day away from the Shire, in about 300 words.

### Structured output: a messy booking email in, a Journey record out
POST http://localhost:8080/shire/journey
Content-Type: text/plain

Subject: Your adventure is booked! Bag End to Mordor (and hopefully back)

Dear FRODO BAGGINS,

Thank you for choosing Middle-earth Travel Co. Your itinerary is below.
Booking reference: MET-3018-RING

DEPARTURE
Bag End, Hobbiton, The Shire
Leaves Wed, Sep 23 at dusk (on foot, pony optional)

STOP 1: BREE
The Prancing Pony
Check-in: 09/29/2026
Confirmation #: PP-0929
Note: a Ranger called Strider will meet you at the bar. Probably.

STOP 2: RIVENDELL
The Last Homely House
Arrives 20 October 2026
Council meeting: Oct 25 (attendance mandatory)
Ref: RIV-1020-ELROND

STOP 3: MORDOR
Mount Doom (day trip)
Arrival: 2027-03-25
Lodging: none available. Travelers are advised not to linger.
Ref: MD-0325

Why walk? Upgrade to Eagle Class for just 39 gold pieces!
Download our app for second-breakfast deals along your route.

You're receiving this because you booked with Middle-earth Travel Co.
Unsubscribe | Privacy Policy
(c) 2026 Middle-earth Travel Co. All rights reserved.


### Bree 1: the gap. The Shire endpoint has no tools, so the model can't know the date.
GET http://localhost:8080/shire/ask
    ?prompt=What is today's date?

### Bree 2: same question with tools. Watch the console for getCurrentDate().
GET http://localhost:8080/bree/ask
    ?prompt=What is today's date?

### Bree 3: the real question. Watch the console for getWeather(Rivendell).
GET http://localhost:8080/bree/ask
    ?prompt=What should I pack for Rivendell?

### Bree 4: watch the model choose. No tools needed, so the console stays quiet.
GET http://localhost:8080/bree/ask
    ?prompt=Tell me a joke about hobbits.
### Rivendell 1: your app as an MCP client. Watch for getWeather(Rivendell), then packing-list.md in journeys/.
GET http://localhost:8080/rivendell/ask
    ?prompt=Check the weather in Rivendell, then save a packing list to packing-list.md

### Mordor: give it a goal, not a question. Watch the console, then route-to-mordor.md in journeys/.
GET http://localhost:8080/mordor/plan
    ?goal=Plan the fastest safe route from Rivendell to Mount Doom and save it to route-to-mordor.md
